(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #103: `is` between two things compares a text field
 by its bytes, not by where they live. Two 5000-byte texts built in two
 different loops are equal; one more byte makes them differ; two empty
 texts, one a literal and one built by a format string, are equal.)

A thing called note has
  a text called body is "".

a note called built.
a note called typed.
Repeat 5000 times,
  Set built's body to "{built's body}y".
a text called piece is "y".
Repeat 4999 times,
  Set piece to "{piece}y".
Set typed's body to piece.
If built is typed then,
  Print "equal across two allocations".
Set typed's body to "{piece}z".
If built is not typed then,
  Print "one more byte differs".
a note called 'first empty'.
a note called 'second empty'.
Set 'second empty''s body to "{'first empty''s body}".
If 'first empty' is 'second empty' then,
  Print "two empty texts are equal".
